  "content": {
    "id": "p26-q6-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "6",
    "prompt": "Miguel’s mother invests $\\$200$ for him each birthday up to and including his 18th birthday. The money earns 6% p.a. How much money will Miguel have on his 18th birthday? Give your answer to the nearest cent.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\$6181.13$",
      "worked": "On the 1st birthday: $200$\n\nOn the 2nd birthday: $200(1.06)+200$\n\nOn the 18th birthday: $200(1.06)^{17}+200(1.06)^{16}+\\cdots+200$\n\nThis is a geometric series with $a=200$, $r=1.06$, $n=18$.\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}FV&=\\frac{200(1.06^{18}-1)}{1.06-1}\\\\FV&\\approx\\$6181.13\\end{aligned}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 39
  },
